## Delete Group

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-delete">DELETE</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/groups/{group_key}</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {your_aio_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/groups/{group_key}
```

```python
```

```cpp
```

```ruby
```

> Response Sample:

```json
{
  "id": 0,
  "key": "string",
  "name": "string",
  "description": "string",
  "feeds": []
}
```

Returns the deleted group.

<aside class="warning">
Deleting a group also deletes every feed that no longer belongs to any group, along with its data. Feeds that are also in another group are kept. The default group (key <code>default</code>) cannot be deleted; trying to returns a 400 error.
</aside>


### Path Parameters

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
username | string | true | a valid username string
group_key | string | true |





